🎗️ 31.9 Why Is Only C Responsible for Count?

This is one of the most important interview questions.

👉 Consider one complete cycle: A → B → C
🔴 When A finishes: A the cycle is incomplete.
🔴 When B finishes: AB the cycle is still incomplete.
🔴 Only after C: ABC has one complete iteration finished.

👉Therefore:

🔴 A → incomplete cycle
🔴 B → incomplete cycle
🔴 C → complete cycle

So:
C
↓
count++ is the natural design.

Important : count represents: Number of complete ABC cycles
It does not represent: number of characters printed
Therefore: C → count++

